{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1342 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "743807ac22fd064b3b2aa744af0eff0e3aaa3a4c79a41bafedfceb20560ea0ed" :edb/db-before-t 1341 :edb/db-after-t 1342 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534654 50 #inst "2026-10-08T03:20:18.781Z" 13194139534654 true] [17592186096353 1100 "Given that\n$\\dfrac{7 x^2 - 2x - 13}{(x^2+1)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{9x+B}{x^2 +1} - \\dfrac{2}{x+1}$,\n\nwhat is the value of $B$?" 13194139534654 false] [17592186096353 1100 "Given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7 x^2 - 2x - 13 }{(x^2+1)(x+1) } = \\dfrac{9x+B}{ x^2 +1} - \\dfrac{2}{x+1} ,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$" 13194139534654 true] [17592186096353 1145 "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x^2+1)(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x^{2} - 2x - 13 &= (9x + B)(x + 1) - 2(x^{2} + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7(0)^{2} - 2(0) - 13 &= (9 \\cdot (0) + B)(0 + 1) - 2((0)^{2} + 1) \\\\\n- 13 &= B - 2 \\\\\nB &= -11\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534654 false] [17592186096353 1145 "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x^2+1)(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{x}^{2}-2x-13 & =(9x+B)(x+1)-2({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)^{2}-2(0)-13 & =(9\\cdot (0)+B)(0+1)-2((0)^{2}+1) \\\\ -13 & =B-2 \\\\ B & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534654 true] [17592186096411 1145 "Our task is to find $A$, $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(2x + 3)/((x^{2} + 4)(x - 1)) &= \\frac{Ax + B}{x^{2} + 4} + \\frac{C}{x - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since $x^2+4$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $(x^2+4)(x-1)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + 3 &= (Ax + B)(x - 1) + C(x^{2} + 4)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(1) + 3 &= (A(1) + B)(1 - 1) + C(1^{2} + 4) \\\\\n5 &= 5C \\\\\nC &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(0) + 3 &= (A(0) + B)(0 - 1) + C(0^{2} + 4) \\\\\n3 &= -B + 4C \\\\\n3 &= -B + 4(1) \\\\\nB &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A$, we choose $x=2$ and use our results for $B$ and $C$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(2) + 3 &= (A(2) + B)(2 - 1) + C(2^{2} + 4) \\\\\n7 &= 2A + B + 8C \\\\\n7 &= 2A + 1 + 8(1) \\\\\n2A &= -2 \\\\\nA &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=-1$, $B=1$, and $C=1$. Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x+3}{(x^2+4)(x-1)} = \\dfrac{1-x}{x^2+4} +\\dfrac{1}{x-1}\n$$" 13194139534654 false] [17592186096411 1145 "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+3}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-1)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+4}+\\frac{C}{x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since $x^2+4$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $(x^2+4)(x-1)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =(Ax+B)(x-1)+C({x}^{2}+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)+3 & =(A(1)+B)(1-1)+C({1}^{2}+4) \\\\ 5 & =5C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)+3 & =(A(0)+B)(0-1)+C({0}^{2}+4) \\\\ 3 & =-B+4C \\\\ 3 & =-B+4(1) \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=2$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2)+3 & =(A(2)+B)(2-1)+C({2}^{2}+4) \\\\ 7 & =2A+B+8C \\\\ 7 & =2A+1+8(1) \\\\ 2A & =-2 \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=-1,$ $B=1,$ and $C=1.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x+3}{(x^2+4)(x-1)} = \\dfrac{1-x}{x^2+4} +\\dfrac{1}{x-1}.\n$$" 13194139534654 true] [17592186096548 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301598 13194139534654 true] [17592186096548 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301612 13194139534654 true] [17592186096605 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301605 13194139534654 true] [17592186097204 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534654 true] [17592186097204 1100 "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nGiven that\n$(5)/((x^{2} + 1)(x + 2)) = \\frac{Ax + B}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{C}{x + 2}$,\nwhere $A$, $B$ and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A + B + C$." 13194139534654 false] [17592186097204 1100 "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x+2)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{C}{x+2},\n$$\n\nwhere $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A+B+C.$" 13194139534654 true] [17592186097204 1145 "We multiply both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+1)(x+2)$ and get\n\n$$\n5=(Ax+B)(x+2)+C({x}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(A(-2)+B)(-2+2)+C((-2)^{2}+1) \\\\ 5 & =5C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(A(0)+B)(0+2)+(1)({0}^{2}+1) \\\\ 5 & =2B+1 \\\\ 2B & =4 \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(A(1)+2)(1+2)+1({1}^{2}+1) \\\\ 5 & =(A+2)(3)+2 \\\\ 3A+6 & =3 \\\\ 3A & =-3 \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=-1,B=2,$ and $C=1.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\nA+B+C=-1+2+1=2.\n$$" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301598 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301599 13194139534654 true] [17592186301598 1089 "q-102558" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301598 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534654 true] [17592186301598 1100 "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}-5x+17}{({x}^{2}+5)(x-2)}=\\frac{Ax-1}{{x}^{2}+5}+\\frac{3}{x-2},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301598 1113 #uuid "fe474dc6-fd17-55a5-b177-03917c5838c0" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301598 1145 "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+5)(x-2)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-5x+17 & =(Ax-1)(x-2)+3({x}^{2}+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1)^{2}-5(1)+17 & =(A(1)-1)(1-2)+3({1}^{2}+5) \\\\ 17 & =(A-1)(-1)+3(6) \\\\ 17 & =-A+1+18 \\\\ -2 & =-A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301599 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301600 13194139534654 true] [17592186301599 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301601 13194139534654 true] [17592186301599 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301602 13194139534654 true] [17592186301599 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301603 13194139534654 true] [17592186301599 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301604 13194139534654 true] [17592186301599 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534654 true] [17592186301599 1041 "selection" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301599 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301601 13194139534654 true] [17592186301599 1110 #uuid "3f38c4c5-e246-5b02-b089-0d899df8b262" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301600 1034 "3" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301600 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534654 true] [17592186301600 1111 #uuid "efd40b21-153e-56ff-b343-99c8aac2ae03" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301601 1034 "2" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301601 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534654 true] [17592186301601 1111 #uuid "89024da1-983c-5a3e-9382-e416645cfce8" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301602 1034 "1" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301602 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534654 true] [17592186301602 1111 #uuid "a7649319-8d95-5cf4-b3c7-6c62ca0bbfa6" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301603 1034 "-4" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534654 true] [17592186301603 1111 #uuid "54874472-e059-576e-a4f3-011d082adcd1" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301604 1034 "-1" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534654 true] [17592186301604 1111 #uuid "8109e3e0-f7d9-51f0-820e-694823ad001c" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301605 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301606 13194139534654 true] [17592186301605 1089 "q-102575" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301605 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534654 true] [17592186301605 1100 "Express $\\frac{6{x}^{2}-8x+5}{({x}^{2}+x+3)(x-4)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." 13194139534654 true] [17592186301605 1113 #uuid "521a4105-19cc-5686-bb26-dc951626ae6d" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301605 1145 "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6{x}^{2}-8x+5}{({x}^{2}+x+3)(x-4)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}+\\frac{C}{(x-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+2x+3$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}+x+3)(x-4)$ and get\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}-8x+5=(Ax+B)(x-4)+C({x}^{2}+x+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(4)^{2}-8(4)+5 & =(A(4)+B)(4-4)+C({4}^{2}+4+3) \\\\ 69 & =23C \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(0)^{2}-8(0)+5 & =(A(0)+B)(0-4)+C({0}^{2}+0+3) \\\\ 5 & =-4B+3C \\\\ 5 & =-4B+3(3) \\\\ 4B & =9-5 \\\\ B & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(1)^{2}-8(1)+5 & =(A(1)+B)(1-4)+C({1}^{2}+1+3) \\\\ 3 & =-3A-3B+5C \\\\ 3 & =-3A-3(1)+5(3) \\\\ 3 & =-3A-3+15 \\\\ 3A & =-3-3+15 \\\\ A & =\\frac{9}{3} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=3,B=1,$ and $C=3.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{6{x}^{2}-8x+5}{({x}^{2}+x+3)(x-4)}=\\frac{3x+1}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}.\n$$" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301606 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301607 13194139534654 true] [17592186301606 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301608 13194139534654 true] [17592186301606 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301609 13194139534654 true] [17592186301606 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301610 13194139534654 true] [17592186301606 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301611 13194139534654 true] [17592186301606 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534654 true] [17592186301606 1041 "selection" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301606 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301607 13194139534654 true] [17592186301606 1110 #uuid "050ca3e5-da3e-5612-80f8-6609b89f3e54" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301607 1034 "\\frac{3x+1}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301607 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534654 true] [17592186301607 1111 #uuid "66ceff31-4de7-5e73-b8f4-617aa95482fa" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301608 1034 "\\frac{3x+4}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)}" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301608 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534654 true] [17592186301608 1111 #uuid "7e17cec5-946b-57b3-93d6-a53a3fbfec68" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301609 1034 "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}-\\frac{5}{(x-4)}" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301609 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534654 true] [17592186301609 1111 #uuid "4d2129c9-cfa0-5852-ad60-250f0f96e996" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301610 1034 "\\frac{x-2}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301610 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534654 true] [17592186301610 1111 #uuid "c7cdb026-7732-59a5-8b47-371bd541f5f2" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301611 1034 "\\frac{2x+3}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)}" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534654 true] [17592186301611 1111 #uuid "2a79315d-acb8-5a84-bf21-49c8b9b0ab8b" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301612 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301613 13194139534654 true] [17592186301612 1089 "q-51144" 13194139534654 true] [17592186301612 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534654 true] [17592186301612 1100 "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+x+3}{({x}^{2}+1)x}=\\frac{Ax+1}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{3}{x},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$" 13194139